                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Skyward Collapse is fucking dangerous.\n\nI work from home, which means this beautiful little bastard is literally within arm's reach at all times. And that is not acceptable for my career.\n\nI can never play this game again. Not because it's bad. Because it's too fucking good. I tell myself, \"I'll just play for five minutes.\" Three hours later, I'm still sitting there, completely unemployed in spirit, while my actual work is slowly decomposing in another browser tab.\n\nSkyward Collapse takes a genre that desperately needed some fucking CPR and gives it a genuinely unique twist. It's clever, addictive, and apparently designed specifically to annihilate whatever remains of my productivity.\nThis isn't a game.\n\nIt's a career-ending productivity grenade. If you work from home, stay the fuck away. Seriously. Don't buy it. Unless you hate having free time, responsibilities, deadlines, and employment.\n\nAbsolutely fucking brilliant.",
